{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Database Testing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Database Testing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ef core database testing ef core database testing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Database Testing.md","fileName":"EF Core Database Testing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EF Core Database Testing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Entity Framework Core Data Access]] [[ASP.NET Core Service Layers and Mapping]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Access","ASP.NET Core Service Layers and Mapping","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Database Testing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Database Testing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ef core database testing ef core database testing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Database Testing.md","fileName":"EF Core Database Testing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EF Core Database Testing","heading":"EF Core Database Testing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"EF Core database testing exercises application behavior with a context configured for a controlled store. The book gives each test a uniquely named in-memory database, creates data through a controller, and retrieves it through the same application path.\n\nThis verifies more than one isolated class and does not reproduce every behavior of the production relational engine. It is fast and repeatable compared with rebuilding a real database, but separate integration evidence is still needed for provider-specific SQL behavior.\n\nFor the layered REST service, replacing the production store with a controlled test databas